1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,700
Hello everyone. You know me, my name is Ishiro Sugata. I'm currently seeking a new assistant.

2
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:14,200
In the age of discovery, Ferdinand Magellan found something significant. The southern route to

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,580
circumnavigate the globe. It was his crowning achievement that using his contemporary ship's

4
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:23,860
logs, he was able to prove that the earth was in fact round. This caused a ripple of panic to

5
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:27,740
course through the network of cartographers of the time. After all, it completely destroyed

6
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:32,440
their concept of the known world and their maps. I believe this type of discovery could happen

7
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:38,440
again now, if we could just somehow seek out this new world. On a side note, Magellan's

8
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:44,820
log also made note of footprints of giants near Patagonia. The possibility exists that whatever

9
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:52,480
he saw still lives on an island somewhere to this very day. What about you? Would you like

10
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:59,480
to be my new assistant? I can hear my heartbeat. How do you think you know?

11
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:01,480
go!

12
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:04,480
I can hear your heartbeat. How do you think you know?

13
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:06,480
I can hear your heartbeat. How do you think you know?

14
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:07,480
Go!

15
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:08,480
Go!

16
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:10,480
Go!

17
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,480
Go!

18
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:14,480
It's a new world that came out! It's huge!

19
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:15,480
Go!

20
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,480
Go!

21
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:17,480
Get up!

22
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:18,480
Go!

23
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:19,480
Go!

24
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,480
Go!

25
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,480
Go!

26
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:23,480
Go!

27
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:24,480
Go!

28
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:25,480
Go!

29
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,480
Go!

30
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,480
Go!

31
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:57,460
I can't hear my heart, but I can't stop.

32
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:27,460
I can't hear my heart, but I can't hear my heart.

33
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:31,400
We're almost to summer vacation, Icarus, and it's getting way hot.

34
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:33,740
I think maybe we're going to have to buy an air conditioner.

35
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:39,240
Master, in looking around us, I think we need to sort out our living conditions first.

36
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:41,160
You might have a point.

37
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:44,920
The entire house went boom thanks to all those damn exploding panties.

38
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:48,820
Hey, I got it.

39
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:51,160
Why don't we just go stay at Sugata's place again?

40
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:52,360
That wasn't so bad.

41
00:02:58,440 --> 00:02:59,600
Yo, Sugata!

42
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:00,800
Hmm?

43
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:05,240
Sorry to drop this on you out of nowhere, but do you mind if we stay here for a while?

44
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:07,360
Sure, knock yourselves out, you two.

45
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:09,400
Seriously? Score!

46
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:11,880
I can't guarantee your safety, though.

47
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:12,340
Huh?

48
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,740
Watch out! Behind you!

49
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:22,160
Bears are all over these parts this time of year.

50
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,980
You really have to watch your backs!

51
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:26,400
This sucks out loud.

52
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:29,220
I'm going to die a miserable death if I stay here.

53
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,680
No way!

54
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:35,400
You stay here and you'll just go sifting through my drawers looking for panties or some crap.

55
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:37,640
I already said you could stay at my place.

56
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:38,800
And get eaten by bears!

57
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:41,500
Yeah, whatever. You probably deserve it.

58
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:42,660
You are such a witch!

59
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:45,700
Childhood friends should help each other out, not wish death upon each other!

60
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:49,060
Promise not to steal my panties even if you're in my room with the perfect opportunity?

61
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:49,700
No.

62
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:50,600
Uh-huh.

63
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,680
Sure, you can count on me.

64
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:53,620
I don't buy it.

65
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,120
Isn't this some joyful banter?

66
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:57,640
What are we doing today?

67
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:00,520
Really?

68
00:04:00,940 --> 00:04:03,360
Well, if that's the case, you're welcome to stay at my house.

69
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:03,840
What?

70
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:07,380
I'll be the sweetest host you could ever hope to have keep you.

71
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,000
Her place is huge, right?

72
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:11,920
People are always saying it's like the biggest one in town or something.

73
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:14,340
Her family are the big shots in Cerami!

74
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:18,160
And why not bring along Sahara and Sugata until your house gets fixed?

75
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:18,940
It'll be fun.

76
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:21,000
Now that sounds like the life.

77
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:31,980
We'll do it!

78
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:32,600
Excellent.

79
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,500
Well, that settles it then.

80
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:36,400
Why don't we get your things moved in?

81
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:38,380
I'll be heading back to my tent.

82
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:40,300
Dude, what's your problem, Sugata?

83
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:42,760
The mopey routine just isn't your style.

84
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,460
Moving up to the big time.

85
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,700
I am Mikako's father.

86
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:53,700
I invite you to stay with us for as long as you wish.

87
00:04:53,700 --> 00:05:03,960
The Satsukitani family has been Cerami City's ruling clan since way back in the Edo period when it was just an in-town.

88
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:07,520
So that's what you meant when you called her family big shots?

89
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:09,660
That's about the shape of it.

90
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:12,600
You guys look freaked.

91
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:14,820
There's nothing to be scared about, I promise.

92
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:19,040
As long as you don't break any of the very specific rules, you'll be fine.

93
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:30,460
She's sorry, really, really sorry.

94
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:32,280
She's just a freaking idiot.

95
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:33,980
Please spare her life, sir.

96
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:41,000
Hey, no big deal.

97
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:45,340
What are you all doing standing around?

98
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:47,780
Hurry up and tend to our honored guests.

99
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,040
Yes, right away, sir.

100
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,160
What a spread!

101
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:58,640
Sir, please try some of this.

102
00:05:58,820 --> 00:06:00,460
Perhaps you'd like some of mine, sir.

103
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:03,240
Have you noticed how they keep calling Sugata, sir?

104
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:08,460
Maybe, I don't know, cause like the Prez and him are all childhood friends or...

105
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:09,220
I don't know.

106
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:14,540
Would you like to take a walk?

107
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,620
What, are you serious?

108
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:26,280
I can't do this anymore.

109
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,840
I can't eat another thing.

110
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:31,760
Where's Master?

111
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:33,600
Ran off to take a bath.

112
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:35,140
Guess all that eating got him all messy.

113
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:35,900
Seriously?

114
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:36,740
He went to bathe?

115
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:37,540
Yeah, why?

116
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:38,260
Is that a problem?

117
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:43,340
No, but it could be the Satsukitani family has something called the Decapitation Bath.

118
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:45,000
It's open only to clan members.

119
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:47,140
He should be fine.

120
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:50,480
As long as Tomoki doesn't try to enter that particular bath.

121
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:58,620
Hello.

122
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:01,140
So you want to hop in with me?

123
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:03,900
I mean, I don't mind.

124
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:05,400
But it might be kind of weird.

125
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:06,480
No, it's cool!

126
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:10,560
You're actually much more forward than I would have given you credit for.

127
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,000
I mean, just walking in here the way you did.

128
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:13,720
N-no!

129
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:19,600
Sorry about this, though.

130
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:23,000
Gotta tell you something serious.

131
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:27,400
You really should hurry up and get the hell out of here.

132
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:30,320
Before someone kills you where you stand.

133
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:30,580
Uh-huh.

134
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:32,940
Oh, God.

135
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:34,260
Intruder alarm!

136
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,540
We have an intruder alarm!

137
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:38,300
There is an intruder in the Decapitation Bath!

138
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,620
After him!

139
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:44,580
There he is!

140
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,000
Get back here!

141
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:50,000
You really think you can get away?

142
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,640
These jerks are going to kill me!

143
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:55,820
Holy crap.

144
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:56,640
Holy crap.

145
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:57,900
Mister, you gotta help!

146
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,860
Please don't let those dudes kill me!

147
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,600
I am sorry, young man.

148
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:04,740
But no matter how close of friends you are with my daughter,

149
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:06,720
our law on this matter is absolute.

150
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,000
Do it!

151
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,580
Tomaki!

152
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:13,620
Why is this happening?

153
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:19,900
The Decapitation Bath was originally a bath for our ancestor, a celestial maiden.

154
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:23,300
It was a place where she could cleanse her divine robe.

155
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:27,480
But after her passing, the bath was open to the public,

156
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:29,860
and Sarami was punished for doing so.

157
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:33,960
Earthquakes, famine, tornadoes.

158
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:39,660
The disasters never ceased until every single person who had visited the bath was decapitated.

159
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:41,840
Since that time,

160
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:46,460
our clan has had the honor of watching over this bath with utmost vigilance

161
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:49,120
in order to protect this fair town of Sarami.

162
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:53,040
Given his friendship with Mikako,

163
00:08:53,660 --> 00:08:54,560
end his life quickly.

164
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:58,520
You can't do this!

165
00:08:58,620 --> 00:09:00,500
Mikako, please make them stop!

166
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:01,140
I cannot.

167
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:03,700
Laws in the Satsukatane family are absolute.

168
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:05,920
Nothing I say would change their minds.

169
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:07,200
But Sugata,

170
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,200
you might be able to.

171
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:14,000
Stop this now!

172
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,300
If you take one more step, then I'll...

173
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,600
Oh, my young Sugata,

174
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:21,180
do you intend on defying the Satsukatane family?

175
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:32,640
This can't be happening.

176
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:33,520
No, please!

177
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:34,920
Please don't kill my friend!

178
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:35,640
Leave my way.

179
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,800
Take out my princess!

180
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,580
Stop this.

181
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:48,500
What are you doing to my master?

182
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:52,040
I asked you a question,

183
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:54,820
and I expect a satisfactory answer.

184
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:17,700
Icarus!

185
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:18,920
Stop it now!

186
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:41,700
I apologize for all the trouble we've caused you.

187
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:43,960
Forget it.

188
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:46,620
I'll overlook everything that happened today

189
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:47,960
on account of that young lady.

190
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:51,140
It appears she's not someone we should be taking lightly.

191
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:53,080
Come on.

192
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:54,120
Let's get out of here.

193
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:55,720
Understood, Master.

194
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:58,940
And don't worry about any of this.

195
00:10:59,200 --> 00:10:59,900
I won't.

196
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:05,340
Mikako,

197
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:09,000
I am going to leave the rest of this matter in your hands.

198
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:11,040
Thank you.

199
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,140
Rise and shine!

200
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:18,720
Good morning, everyone!

201
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,180
Good morning to you two.

202
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:25,600
We're almost there,

203
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:26,980
so you better wake the heck up.

204
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:27,440
Where?

205
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:29,080
To the uninhabited island.

206
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:29,880
Huh?

207
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:39,000
What the hell is going on?

208
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:39,340
What the hell is going on?

209
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:53,220
Wow, it's gorgeous.

210
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:56,960
This is a private island owned by my family.

211
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:59,700
I want you all to treat this place as your own home.

212
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,000
Just out of curiosity,

213
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:03,460
why'd you drag us to the middle of nowhere anyway?

214
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:06,420
Because a certain someone broke a sacred family law,

215
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:08,000
which has made it all a wee bit tense

216
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,440
staying back at the main house.

217
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:12,660
I would have felt awful tossing you out onto the street,

218
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:13,960
so I brought you here instead.

219
00:12:14,260 --> 00:12:16,020
I hope that wasn't the wrong thing to do.

220
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:18,060
I could always take you back.

221
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,500
No, this is great.

222
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:20,580
Seriously, thanks.

223
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,580
You've gone really far out of your way for Tomoki,

224
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:23,280
haven't you?

225
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:24,560
Tomo,

226
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:26,920
you better show her some pretty serious gratitude.

227
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:28,840
Thank you, Prez.

228
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:30,900
You're welcome, Tomoki.

229
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,600
Well, since we're here,

230
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:36,560
let's go swimming.

231
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:37,540
Hold off for a second.

232
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:40,820
Don't underestimate uninhabited islands.

233
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:41,580
Before anything,

234
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,820
we need to secure a food source for our survival.

235
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:44,440
What?

236
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,500
Mikako said this is her family's island.

237
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:48,660
Isn't there some kind of cottage or bungalow?

238
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:50,700
Actually, we've got nothing at all.

239
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:53,040
And that's our situation.

240
00:12:53,540 --> 00:12:55,820
So we can't afford to spend time sunning and swimming.

241
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:58,480
Why don't we leave finding the food to Icarus and Tomoki?

242
00:12:58,740 --> 00:12:59,740
The rest of us will head out

243
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:01,040
to look for fresh drinking water.

244
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:02,460
Sure, sounds good.

245
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:05,420
Hey, Icarus.

246
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:07,040
Yes, Master?

247
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:09,060
Think maybe you should jump in the water

248
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:11,260
and catch us some bream or tuna or something tasty?

249
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:12,140
What do you say?

250
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:13,800
Yes, Master.

251
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:17,000
Make sure you catch some fat ones with a lot of meat on them.

252
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,040
Yes, Master.

253
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:27,340
Cool, I found a coconut crab.

254
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:29,540
Coconut crab sounds awesome.

255
00:13:29,780 --> 00:13:31,140
I've always wanted to try one.

256
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:32,420
Here goes.

257
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:37,180
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

258
00:13:37,260 --> 00:13:37,920
Please forgive me.

259
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:38,820
I don't want to eat you.

260
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:39,320
I don't.

261
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:46,060
This sucks balls.

262
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:48,840
On the verge of death because of some stupid crab.

263
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:50,960
Maybe we eat vegetarian this trip.

264
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:55,140
Man, I'm freaking starving.

265
00:13:55,140 --> 00:13:59,860
Okay, clearly these mushrooms are a bad idea.

266
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:01,240
Oh, well.

267
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:02,220
No choice.

268
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:08,240
No way, sister.

269
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:09,280
Shut up!

270
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:10,220
Grandpa!

271
00:14:10,740 --> 00:14:11,300
Grandpa!

272
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:27,600
Holy crap.

273
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:29,620
Must have passed out after I eat that thing.

274
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:37,200
What the hell is this?

275
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:41,060
Save me!

276
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:42,160
Zahara!

277
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,040
Oh, my gosh.

278
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:50,640
No!

279
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:51,800
Zahara!

280
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:55,880
How did you get down here?

281
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:56,700
Are you okay?

282
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:00,900
I'm glad you're safe.

283
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:03,300
I was starting to get so worried about you.

284
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:04,680
What happened?

285
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,280
I thought you were with the others.

286
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,420
Where are they?

287
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:08,880
I don't know what happened to them.

288
00:15:09,040 --> 00:15:11,160
Once we started running, we all got separated.

289
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:15,600
What's that?

290
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:19,520
That sound was chasing us, so we ran as fast as we could.

291
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:21,060
I'm scared, Tomaki.

292
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:25,060
We'll find a safe place to hide and sort out what's going on.

293
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:26,260
Calm down, Zahara.

294
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:26,920
I've got you.

295
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,340
We're gonna be fine.

296
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:32,160
When the sun comes up, we'll go search for everyone else.

297
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:32,600
Cool?

298
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:33,800
Cool.

299
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:42,500
When morning broke, we went looking for Prez, Sugata, and Icarus.

300
00:15:43,340 --> 00:15:47,460
But one day turned into two, then turned into three, four, who knows how many.

301
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:48,980
We never found them.

302
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:51,940
But at night, we kept hearing the howl.

303
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:54,440
An awful, terrifying howl.

304
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:55,100
Oh, no.

305
00:15:55,640 --> 00:15:56,740
What if they're all dead?

306
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:58,900
What if they got eaten by that horrible thing?

307
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:00,520
They'll be fine.

308
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:01,680
I just know it.

309
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:04,000
No way they'd go down so easy.

310
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:05,160
Yes, you're right.

311
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:09,660
I mean, I'm sure Prez would have called for help on her radio by now.

312
00:16:09,660 --> 00:16:11,280
Yeah.

313
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:21,580
Check it out!

314
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:25,140
Wow, that's a pretty big catch for breakfast.

315
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:27,240
Just hand him over and I'll cook him up.

316
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:27,960
Cool.

317
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:29,080
Sounds good to me.

318
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:30,540
You want one bowl?

319
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:32,220
And so an entire month passed.

320
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:32,800
What do you think?

321
00:16:33,060 --> 00:16:35,640
The two of us completely readjusted to life on the island.

322
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:38,140
So how I even started smiling again.

323
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:44,240
But just when I started thinking it wouldn't be all bad if things went on like this forever.

324
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:54,780
What's the matter?

325
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:55,680
Are you all right?

326
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:57,960
I'm sorry.

327
00:16:58,180 --> 00:17:02,520
I just started thinking about everybody else and got kind of sad.

328
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:08,580
It makes me wonder, what's going to happen if no one ever comes to rescue us?

329
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:10,280
Will we just live here forever?

330
00:17:14,120 --> 00:17:17,300
I guess we'll have to make the most of the time we have together.

331
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:21,020
But with me here, at least you won't be lonely.

332
00:17:22,660 --> 00:17:25,640
And I promise you now, you'll never be sad.

333
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:27,300
Thank you, Tomaki.

334
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:44,240
And you know, I'm thinking life wouldn't be near as depressing as it is now if we had kids.

335
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:46,280
You want to have kids?

336
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:47,300
You mean like now?

337
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:50,580
No, that's not what I was trying to say at all.

338
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,300
I meant to...

339
00:17:52,300 --> 00:18:00,460
Um, Zahara.

340
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:04,880
I... It's okay, Tomaki.

341
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,600
We gotta get out of here.

342
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:26,560
Yeah.

343
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:32,200
Zahara!

344
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:38,320
Dammit, legs.

345
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:39,420
You have to move.

346
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:40,720
Do you hear me?

347
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:41,920
I said move!

348
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:43,640
Tomaki.

349
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:46,700
Don't worry about me.

350
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:48,220
I promise.

351
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,040
I'll be just fine.

352
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:51,520
I will.

353
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:51,580
I will.

354
00:18:56,560 --> 00:19:04,260
Let her go, monster!

355
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:10,320
Let go of her, dammit!

356
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:15,060
Let her go!

357
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,700
Let her go!

358
00:19:17,540 --> 00:19:21,140
Get your tentacles off her, you damn dirty beast!

359
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:37,320
I have returned with a fish, master.

360
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:42,200
I did not find many schools of tuna out here, so I crossed over to the southern hemisphere

361
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,100
to find this one.

362
00:19:43,100 --> 00:19:46,920
Tomo, I think this is just seaweed and oysters.

363
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,420
It's what?

364
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:51,480
So they were just stuck all over Icarus like barnacles or something?

365
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:52,320
Yes.

366
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:56,640
As I walked along the ocean floor, all of that became stuck to me for some reason.

367
00:19:57,480 --> 00:19:59,900
So what was that blood-curdling howl you let out?

368
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:01,280
And where are the others?

369
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:05,520
Master, do you wish for me to check for their life signs on my radar?

370
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:07,220
Yes, please do!

371
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:08,420
One moment.

372
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:27,380
Ha!

373
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:32,600
Ha!

374
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,040
Now that's entertainment!

375
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:37,200
It's also your punishment for breaking the rules of my family.

376
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:39,200
And with that, I will exonerate him.

377
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:42,200
And I promise you now, you'll never be sad.

378
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:45,200
Thank you, Tomaki.

379
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:49,200
Oh, to be young and in love.

380
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:51,200
Well, I think it had more to do with the fact

381
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:53,200
that his life had recently been spared.

382
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:55,200
You're telling me all this crap?

383
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:58,200
All this happened because of something Tomaki did again?

384
00:20:58,200 --> 00:21:01,200
Whoa, just calmed down, Sohara.

385
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:03,200
This whole thing was your fault, Tomo!

386
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:06,200
You're the biggest jerk on planet Earth!

387
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:09,200
Somebody help me!

388
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:17,200
It's like my house never even exploded.

389
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,200
What the hell?

390
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:20,200
Master, look over there.

391
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:23,200
Presents Icarus Breeding!

392
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,200
Hello!

393
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,200
Please accept this small token.

394
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:32,200
A gift from the entire Satsukatune family to you.

395
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:34,200
You may not have known this,

396
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:36,200
but strength counts for everything in my family.

397
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:41,200
And it looks like my father has grown rather attached to Icarus here.

398
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:42,200
Icarus Breeding!

399
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,200
Icarus Breeding!

400
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,200
Icarus Breeding!

401
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:46,200
Icarus Breeding!

402
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,200
Icarus Breeding!

403
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,200
Icarus Breeding!

404
00:21:48,200 --> 00:22:18,180
We'll be right back.

405
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:48,180
We'll be right back.

406
00:22:48,200 --> 00:23:18,180
We'll be right back.

407
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:48,180
We'll be right back.

